  "namingIssues": null,
  "existingDescription": "A container that lays out two Button instances together and controls how they sit in the available width. Five alignment variants cover Justify, Start, End, Center and Stack, and each button can be switched off independently. PURPOSE: Groups related actions, such as a primary and a secondary choice, into one block with consistent spacing. Keywords: actions. BEHAVIOUR: The group itself is not interactive. Interaction sits in the nested Button instances. Align changes the distribution of the children: Justify spreads them across the full width, Start, End and Center pack them to one side, and Stack places them one above the other. Button Start and Button End hide or show the first and second button, so the group can render a single action. COMPOSITION: Two Button instances, each made of a text label and two container instances that sit before and after the label. The container instances hold the omitted leading and trailing content. AI code generators should look for existing Button and container implementations in the development codebase before writing new ones. USAGE: Use when two actions appear side by side, for example in a dialog footer, a form or a card. Use Justify when the group fills a fixed-width panel, Start or End for inline toolbars, and Stack on narrow layouts where side-by-side buttons would be cramped. For a single action, place the Button on its own rather than hiding one side of this group. CODE GENERATION NOTES: Implement as a flex container with a direction switch for Stack and a justify-content switch for the other four values. Gap comes from Space/200, Space/300 and Space/400, so expose it as a token, not a literal. Keep DOM order fixed and let CSS handle alignment, so the tab order stays the same across variants. The two buttons differ in emphasis: one uses Background/Brand/Default with Text/Brand/On Brand, the other uses Text/Neutral/Default with Stroke/Border. Map these to existing button variants rather than re-styling. Hiding a button should remove it from the DOM, not just hide it visually.\n\nNote\nButton variants, states and sizes come for the original Button Component",
